 * returned in the `X-New-Access-Token` response header. If neither token can
 * be validated the middleware throws an `HTTPException` with status `401`.
 *
 * @param {object} options - The options for the JWT refresh middleware.
 * @param {SignatureKey} options.secret - A value of your secret key used to verify the access token.
 * @param {SignatureAlgorithm} options.alg - The algorithm used for verifying both tokens.
 * @param {SignatureKey} [options.refreshSecret] - Secret used to verify the refresh token. Defaults to `secret`.
 * @param {string} [options.refreshCookie='refresh_token'] - Name of the cookie that stores the refresh token.
 * @param {(payload: unknown) => Promise<string>} options.onRefresh - Callback that receives the verified refresh-token payload and must return a new access token.
 * @returns {MiddlewareHandler} The middleware handler function.
